# Vendored runtimes (CPython + npm) fetched at build time by
# scripts/fetch-runtimes.mjs — large binaries, never committed.
resources/runtime/

# electron-vite temp config
electron.vite.config.*.mjs

# Agent CLI harness folders. Everything in them is written on whichever machine
# runs the agent: harness settings (`enabledPlugins`, absolute socket and
# Electron paths in `.cursor/`), skills copied in by the studio installer or
# the harness's own plugin installs (each stamped with `installedAt`), and
# agent-state hooks rendered from templates under resources/. None of it is
# source, and ignoring the folders whole stops every new install from turning
# up as untracked noise.
.claude/
.cursor/
.grok/
.opencode/
.agents/
.mcp.json
# ...except the one the app SHIPS. `.mcp.json` above is unanchored, so it matches
# at every depth, and the SprintEngine Studio plugin's own server declaration is
# a source file, not a generated workspace config.
!resources/studio-plugin/**/.mcp.json

# Everything the app writes into a workspace's own sidecar directory — this
# checkout's included, because the app is developed in the app. All of it is
# runtime state: the backlog link cache (resolved link statuses, the agent
# terminal holding an item, module metadata bound to a live session — every
# value re-derived from the world, so deleting it costs a lookup and never
# data); Debug Mode's scratch file per agent terminal; browser tab screenshots
# and element crops; captured conversation transcripts and review state;
# automation runtime state.
#
# BOTH names are listed. The directory was `.multi-code/` before the app was
# renamed (2026-09-08) and is `.sprintengine/` now, and nothing migrates a
# workspace that already has the old one — so both are live for as long as both
# are read, and a checkout keeping the old name must not start showing its
# runtime state as untracked noise for someone to eventually commit.
#
# `backlog/config.json` is in here too, and is NOT an exception. It carries the
# `MC` item-key prefix, so it reads like project configuration, but the app
# rewrites it as it runs and a clone gets its own on first run — tracking it
# published one machine's live state, which is the same mistake
# `backlog/items.json` made before it.
# No exceptions under either name: a re-include here only holds a door open for
# a workspace's live runtime state to be committed by someone who added a file
# and saw git offer it.
.sprintengine/
.multi-code/

# Editor directories and files
.idea
.vscode
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# SprintEngine Studio's own plugin: install output, built from
# `resources/studio-plugin/`, which IS tracked. (The skill packs its installer
# copies into each harness's skill dir are covered by the harness folders above.)
.multicode/studio-plugin/

# The agent-state reporter script. `AGENT_STATE_HOOK_SCRIPT_REL` in
# src/main/agent-state.ts is `.multicode/hooks/agent-state.mjs`: the app copies
# `resources/hooks/multicode-agent-state.mjs` there byte for byte when it opens a
# workspace, so the tracked copy was a second, staler original.
.multicode/hooks/

# Leftover app metadata from the retired Design Wizard (deleted 2026-09-08):
# its idea seed and inspiration drops. Nothing writes here any more, and the
# files on an existing workspace are deliberately left alone, so the ignore
# stays until those workspaces are gone.
.guided-brief/

# Scratch output of the Playwright MCP server an agent session may run against
# this checkout (screenshots, console logs). Not the retired Playwright test
# harnesses, which are gone; this is another tool's cache.
.playwright-mcp/

# The source-build-only trusted marketplace publishers (DESIGN D2). A
# first-party module id is publisher-locked to the release signing key, so a
# contributor building from source cannot install their own build of one
# without adding their own dev public key here. It is unioned into the trusted
# set ONLY when the app is not packaged (src/main/marketplace/trusted-publishers.ts),
# it is never read by the registry verifier, and a committed copy would be a
# second signing authority shipped to every user.
resources/marketplace/trusted-publishers.dev.json

# The backlog lives outside the checkout. It is planning material, not source:
# it names unshipped work, priorities and rationale, and a public repository is
# the wrong place for it. Each machine points at its own folder through
# `backlog/config.json` in the workspace sidecar (`root`), which is ignored with
# the rest of that directory, so the location never ships either.
#
# Nothing in the build reads it: the frontmatter round-trip property tests use a
# checked-in fixture corpus under src/shared/backlog/__fixtures__/ rather than
# this repository's own items.
backlog/
